<http://data.silknow.org/object/705efac1-c9fb-3c13-b49e-13faa9228d5c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning, surface darning on the diagonal and running stitch, backed with silk faced with bias-cut cotton. Displayed and analysed under glass.\nWhite ground with slightly diagonal rows in which a lobed mushroom lozenge containing a light blue octagon and pink swastika and four yellow 'eaves', alternating with a horizontal light blue lozenge containing a pink Z-motif. On the left hand side one of these lozenges has a green and one has a pink ground with a yellow z-motif.  The other row has a yellow 8-pointed star with 4 sperm-like attachments alternating with a vertical blue lozenge and pink Z-motif. The border might have a light green ground and contains a yellow diagonal leaf-shaped motif either side of a pink Y-motif which alternates direction.\nThreads: 2S silk: light blue, mushroom, pink, yellow, light green, black and white. The outlines are worked in blocks in black running stitch.\nBacking: said to be purple silk\nFacing: light blue cotton with a fine dark blue check."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, packed design of star-medallions, yellow stars and light blue diamonds on cream ground, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1750-1825"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c4048537-99d0-3e99-a16c-4a041868a6a3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c951fbcc-9123-31fd-8676-713baf14e64c> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, packed design of star-medallions, yellow stars and light blue diamonds on cream ground, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1750-1825"@en , "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning, surface darning on the diagonal and running stitch, backed with silk faced with bias-cut cotton. Displayed and analysed under glass.\nWhite ground with slightly diagonal rows in which a lobed mushroom lozenge containing a light blue octagon and pink swastika and four yellow 'eaves', alternating with a horizontal light blue lozenge containing a pink Z-motif. On the left hand side one of these lozenges has a green and one has a pink ground with a yellow z-motif.  The other row has a yellow 8-pointed star with 4 sperm-like attachments alternating with a vertical blue lozenge and pink Z-motif. The border might have a light green ground and contains a yellow diagonal leaf-shaped motif either side of a pink Y-motif which alternates direction.\nThreads: 2S silk: light blue, mushroom, pink, yellow, light green, black and white. The outlines are worked in blocks in black running stitch.\nBacking: said to be purple silk\nFacing: light blue cotton with a fine dark blue check."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/705efac1-c9fb-3c13-b49e-13faa9228d5c/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/705efac1-c9fb-3c13-b49e-13faa9228d5c/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "127-1901" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O159120> .

