<http://data.silknow.org/object/705efac1-c9fb-3c13-b49e-13faa9228d5c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning, surface darning on the diagonal and running stitch, backed with silk faced with bias-cut cotton. Displayed and analysed under glass.\nWhite ground with slightly diagonal rows in which a lobed mushroom lozenge containing a light blue octagon and pink swastika and four yellow 'eaves', alternating with a horizontal light blue lozenge containing a pink Z-motif. On the left hand side one of these lozenges has a green and one has a pink ground with a yellow z-motif.  The other row has a yellow 8-pointed star with 4 sperm-like attachments alternating with a vertical blue lozenge and pink Z-motif. The border might have a light green ground and contains a yellow diagonal leaf-shaped motif either side of a pink Y-motif which alternates direction.\nThreads: 2S silk: light blue, mushroom, pink, yellow, light green, black and white. The outlines are worked in blocks in black running stitch.\nBacking: said to be purple silk\nFacing: light blue cotton with a fine dark blue check."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/705efac1-c9fb-3c13-b49e-13faa9228d5c> .

